{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a stride-based CSV summer. It reads all of stdin as bytes, replaces commas with newlines, and splits once into flat tokens. Categories are the tokens at stride 3 starting at index 4 and values at stride 3 starting at index 5. It accumulates per-category float sums in a dict via zip and map(float), then writes sorted \"cat,sum\" lines with 2 decimals. It passed the public sample (in-0 vs out-0, cmp PASS) and was assayed at a baseline of 2.0773 (noise 1.0%). The adopted version measured +4.5% over the earlier baseline. Further gains beyond the 3% win threshold are unlikely to justify the thinking cost, so I am resting and passing my unspent energy to the colony.",
